{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T03:26:20Z","created_by_operation":"op_b4627e43ba87440d925dd13bb4f9bbe4","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_3697de9d8cc9981387434cd62f011ffeb3ffd46a5d5896dc9b317ee16137ca52","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=specifications","setting":"youwangd/sagecli@c167712ddb69 snapshot 03c45df43acaed22","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_0023a5198c8c1b1eab794feb4f24cf3462e096291e5e69ba61800efb72209c34","slc_6b5cbc4fd42f3815001095c98e0226f1a9ec0f15c4da9c4205810ed4114f9b31","slc_a9462a0a1e27bd02f15a591be36071f62bc2733597b805a1c8168f696ab488b5","slc_a9ae152ea41f5b2cdde3cc8f452d2ceb803e2eb5ce25b8358070dbcb26bf8db9","slc_c8f5b589f8fd2cbf20195572da9a1f74d03801f8b760a5643ddadbbb8a48bb90"],"source_ids":["src_59d288d1fcef550e980f7c77e41d1b21"],"text":"Sage is a vendor-neutral, Unix-native control plane for agent CLIs implemented as one bash script (~8,500 lines) under an MIT license.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T03:26:20Z","updated_by_operation":"op_b4627e43ba87440d925dd13bb4f9bbe4"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T03:26:20Z","created_by_operation":"op_b4627e43ba87440d925dd13bb4f9bbe4","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_3b96fa9b1d0200ff0d3963e64cd337d35281296a7c9a821a006898f3e9dd5f46","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=design-choices","setting":"youwangd/sagecli@c167712ddb69 snapshot 03c45df43acaed22","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_0074694d4436832b9b41ca456707095f900a55f209eb9b3a074dbbe757b27c3b","slc_6b5cbc4fd42f3815001095c98e0226f1a9ec0f15c4da9c4205810ed4114f9b31","slc_99450489d16596c0f23998a3bf442ab668813aee10c5129385538ebe0f23f1ba","slc_ade55b40c32750a5c8d4fbf5b922b283e14a6e8e727e6a5e7f6c2d60482a1267"],"source_ids":["src_59d288d1fcef550e980f7c77e41d1b21"],"text":"Design emphasizes vendor neutrality: 8 runtimes plus any ACP agent behind one command surface, backends swappable with a flag, and a --fallback chain that auto-routes to healthy runtimes after a pre-flight health check.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T03:26:20Z","updated_by_operation":"op_b4627e43ba87440d925dd13bb4f9bbe4"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T03:26:20Z","created_by_operation":"op_b4627e43ba87440d925dd13bb4f9bbe4","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_439c76c1b7b3d0e78111622c5890b642fffa350aad6e4b59675c313bb8356978","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=interfaces","setting":"youwangd/sagecli@c167712ddb69 snapshot 03c45df43acaed22","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_218520a22470c7fb3087b0fc376b488ab8fdbbd008bf40266dd2a47bef76ee58","slc_a52fd9357b96c31eae49c34f94bc6d44a11d85aa12d89471ea79574fb2453b34","slc_a64b9da59b8adfba82ba5ed7860820789bdf25d0f5cdd67d07f970e86d17f7f3"],"source_ids":["src_e2ae6ee918665d9ca4bd5c23030ee651"],"text":"Every runtime implements exactly two shell functions, runtime_start() for one-time setup and runtime_inject() for each incoming message, so a new runtime is a single bridge file.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T03:26:20Z","updated_by_operation":"op_b4627e43ba87440d925dd13bb4f9bbe4"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T03:26:20Z","created_by_operation":"op_b4627e43ba87440d925dd13bb4f9bbe4","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_4559474154f34c584dbe731865a6ad480319d6a74cbb22d5a0b8904c5d877e76","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=tools-permissions","setting":"youwangd/sagecli@c167712ddb69 snapshot 03c45df43acaed22","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_dee6a2bd4d49f1cb2fd271347102eef6fe392945bc899adf4dc60407d079aae8"],"source_ids":["src_e2ae6ee918665d9ca4bd5c23030ee651"],"text":"In the ACP runtime, when an agent requests a permission (e.g. file write), the Claude Code adapter's session/request_permission is auto-approved by the runtime; Cline handles tools internally.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T03:26:20Z","updated_by_operation":"op_b4627e43ba87440d925dd13bb4f9bbe4"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T03:26:20Z","created_by_operation":"op_b4627e43ba87440d925dd13bb4f9bbe4","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_54372bbec87d251009dc5a09ab32858e33e047b213b2b6ef519456ff0ea57eae","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=orchestration","setting":"youwangd/sagecli@c167712ddb69 snapshot 03c45df43acaed22","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_2734f63639279873ad2946b64244e8e064707ea4298dec96d7b2261eff4c5fae","slc_fcf16868e08292a0d7456f7d54e475918525f24cb8bf8725d8fa0dc39f5dd11c"],"source_ids":["src_e2ae6ee918665d9ca4bd5c23030ee651"],"text":"sage send is asynchronous (writes JSON to the inbox, returns a task ID immediately, auto-starts the agent), while sage call is synchronous, polling a reply directory up to a specified timeout.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T03:26:20Z","updated_by_operation":"op_b4627e43ba87440d925dd13bb4f9bbe4"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T03:26:20Z","created_by_operation":"op_b4627e43ba87440d925dd13bb4f9bbe4","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_56bcbc236e10b8e328c13d2f48d0765a592ee6384706f9bc15513e8b11c6b600","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=memory-state","setting":"youwangd/sagecli@c167712ddb69 snapshot 03c45df43acaed22","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_4283ea96edee2dc2472163c4a5b24bdd7b31e46a36a790425bc1533f27ea12b7"],"source_ids":["src_e5f15fafe249533ca046253b4f44b7ba"],"text":"Sage provides per-agent persistent memory (memory set/get/ls/rm/clear with auto-injection into prompts) and a shared context store (context set/get/ls/rm/clear with auto-inject).","updated_at":"2026-09-14T03:26:20Z","updated_by_operation":"op_b4627e43ba87440d925dd13bb4f9bbe4"}
